ys it prefers the lottery with the more favorable sum — meaning less negative. So A has a more favorable sum of outcome differences (since -1000 is better than 0, if that were the case). But there is no other outcome. Thus, the sum of pairwise differences is just -1000, and A has the lower loss. So the reason would prefer A. The information is applicable and derivable from the lotteries.",
